      "stdout": "Run AI frame interpolation for a target video segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --wait TEXT         Wait for the algorithm to finish: true / false (default true)\r\n          --timeout <duration> \r\n                              Execution timeout; explicit unit required, e.g. 5min or 300s\r\n          --fps TEXT:{30,50,60} REQUIRED \r\n                              Target frame rate for AI frame interpolation: 30 / 50 / 60\r\n          --model TEXT:{client,cloud} \r\n                              AI frame interpolation model: client (default) / cloud\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Run client-side AI frame interpolation to 50 fps\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-frame-interpolation --seg-id <UUID> --fps 50 --model client --wait true\r\n  # Submit cloud AI frame interpolation and wait for the product\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-frame-interpolation --seg-id <UUID> --fps 60 --model cloud --timeout 10min\r\n",
